Reason: decode ordinary AAC (AAC-LC, HE-AAC v1 and v2) with AudioToolbox, not
only xHE-AAC, because our FFmpeg has no AAC decoder (plan.md §3.3).
- CanUseAudioToolbox() accepts every AAC profile.
- The converter's input is kAudioFormatMPEG4AAC, configured from an 'esds'
  magic cookie around the AudioSpecificConfig (built for AAC-LC if a stream
  has none), and the best playable layer is chosen with
  kAudioFormatProperty_FormatList / FirstPlayableFormatFromList so HE-AAC's
  SBR and PS layers are decoded.
- ADTS headers (added by MSE's MP4 parser and present in MPEG-2 TS/ADTS) are
  skipped; AudioToolbox wants raw frames.
- The loudness and DRC settings stay xHE-AAC only.
Our own code, written from Chromium's file and Apple's AudioToolbox
documentation; Vivaldi's LGPL audiotoolboxdec.c was not used. BSD-3, like
the file it patches. No upstream bug.

